{
	"$description": "The icons avenCEO draws. Geometry only — a viewBox and path data, validated when the registry loads. Colour comes from currentColor, which is why an icon works in both themes without a second file. DUOTONE throughout: a filled backing shape at 0.2 under the stroked figure, so the set reads as one family with the Phosphor-duotone social glyphs rather than as two icon languages in one product. Both opacities are the same colour, which is what keeps a duotone icon themeable — two colours would not be. Each figure is INSET inside its backing, so the stroke has room to breathe instead of running to the backing edge — a hamburger filling its slab reads as cramped rather than as a pair. The amount is per icon because a glyph that fills its box needs more than one already small inside its shape. Drawn on the lucide 24 grid at stroke width 2, so a thirteenth icon can be lifted from lucide and given a backing without redrawing the figure.",
